msgid ""
"Create a JS script to translate the result data object into an array "
"containing objects with properties 'name' and 'value'. The input data is "
"provided as 'data' and the result should be put on the global variable "
"'results'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:63
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:74
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:130
msgid "**Example:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:65
msgid ""
"for(var x=0;x < data.length; x++) {\n"
"  results.push({name: data[x].name,value:data[x].id});\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:71
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:327
msgid "REQUEST SCRIPT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:72
msgid ""
"Create a JS script to prepare the request. Return a data object as the "
"body for a POST request, and return an array containing properties 'name'"
" and 'value' for a GET request. The input data is provided as 'data' and "
"the result should be put on the global variable 'results'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:76
#, python-brace-format
msgid "results.push({name: 'userId', value : data.users})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:80
msgid ""
"In a GET request (SOURCE METHOD = GET), the value of the results variable"
" is used to build out the request parameters. Thus, in the example "
"``results`` value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:82
#, python-brace-format
msgid "results=[{name:\"name1\",value: \"value1\"}]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:86
msgid "The request would be made to: ``https://<someURL>?name1=value1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:88
msgid ""
"In a POST request (SOURCE METHOD = POST), the value of the results "
"variable is used to build the body of the POST request. Thus, in the "
"example ``results`` value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:90
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"results=[{name:\"name1\", value:\"value1\"}, {name:\"name2\", "
"value:\"value2\"}]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:94
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:116
msgid "The following JSON body would be posted to the target URL:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:96
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{name:\"name1\", value:\"value1\"}, {name:\"name2\", value:\"value2\"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:100
msgid ""
"An alternative method to building the POST request (SOURCE METHOD = "
"POST), can be seen below.  As well, we can access other **Inputs** that "
"are available on the same form, when provisioning an Instance or Catalog "
"Item. As seen below, the other Inputs can be accessed using the ``data`` "
"variable.  We can access another Input by calling its **Field Name**, "
"which can be configured when editing the Input in |LibOptInp|.  This "
"allows using data from other Inputs to be used in this Input's request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:104
msgid ""
"In the example below the Input Field Name we'll access is "
"``myinputfieldname``, which we can get either the name (visible value for"
" lists) or value from the item:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:106
msgid ""
"Name variable:  ``data.myinputfieldname`` Value variable:  "
"``data.myinputfieldname_value``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:109
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"var postBody = {};\n"
"postBody[\"number\"] = data.myinputfieldname_value;\n"
"postBody[\"env\"] = \"all\";\n"
"results = postBody;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:118
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{ \"number\": \"123456\", \"env\": \"all\" }"
msgstr ""

